content.text:
I'll work through this step by step: find Sam Rivera's user ID, the Platform team ID, the "In Review" workflow state, then find and update the matching issues.

Let me start by gathering the needed IDs.

<thinking>
I need to find:
1. Sam Rivera's user ID
2. The Platform team's ID
3. The "In Review" workflow state ID

I can query all three in a single GraphQL request to be efficient.
</thinking>

<action>
curl -s -X POST https://api.linear.app/graphql \
  -H "Authorization: <TOKEN>" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{
    "query": "
    query {
      users(includeDisabled: false) {
        nodes {
          id
          name
          displayName
        }
      }
      teams {
        nodes {
          id
          name
          key
        }
      }
      workflowStates(includeArchived: false) {
        nodes {
          id
          name
          type
          team {
            id
            name
          }
        }
      }
    }"
  }'
</action>

